\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nTicker: MEDP | Sector: Healthcare | Industry: Diagnostics & Research\nArchetype: B (Quality Compounder) with material Cyclical (C) exposure \u2014 classifiable as a transition watch toward C if H2-2026 implied deceleration persists.\nPrimary Engine: Engine 1 (Traditional DCF + Multiples)\nCross-Check Engine: Engine 2 (Cycle-Adjusted / Normalized Earnings)\nData coverage: Tier 1 (SEC filings, 11 fiscal years + 10 quarters) is strong. Gaps: no segment detail, no investments line, no consolidated tax-rate identity, debt-component overlap unresolved, analyst Q&A not held. Model confidence: MODERATE (downgraded from High by litigation overhang, unresolved debt mapping, and the 4.6% implied H2-2026 growth inflection).\nCentral findings:\n  \u2013 FY2026 raised guidance midpoint implies H2-2026 revenue growth of ~4.6% YoY versus +32.0% in Q4-2025 and +21.7% H1-2026 [Arithmetic on Actual guidance and Actual quarterly history].\n  \u2013 Record Q2-2026 bookings (net book-to-bill 1.13x, $795.7M net new awards) and backlog $3,014.2M (+4.9% YoY) are real positives but convert slowly: only $1.96B of backlog is expected to convert over the next 12 months, versus TTM revenue of $2.782B [Actual, company release].\n  \u2013 A securities-fraud class action (Case No. 1:26-cv-00346) is pending, alleging understated cancellations and overstated book-to-bill; lead-plaintiff deadline passed 2026-06-08 [Actual from law-firm disclosures; allegations unproven].\n  \u2013 Normalized owner FCF power is ~$400\u2013450M [Estimate], implying the market is paying ~38\u201343x normalized FCF at T0.\n  \u2013 Base intrinsic value: ~$300/share [Estimate]. T0 price $620.75. Margin of safety: \u2013107% (none). Expected 2-year fair value: ~$301/share [Estimate]. Verdict: S/SELL (avoid; risk/reward asymmetric to the downside).\n\nSECTION 1. MACRO CONTEXT\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25