+20   | 35  | 449       |\n| 2027 | +7.5% [Estimate: consensus 6.1% [Agg] + demand] | 3,058 | 21.0% [Assumption] | 642 | 507 | 32 | 45 | +10 | 37 | 447 |\n| 2028 | +6.5% [Estimate: industry 5.5\u20137% (Persistence/Arizton [Estimate])] | 3,257 | 21.0% [Assumption] | 684 | 540 | 34 | 48 | +8 | 38 | 480 |\n| 2029 | +5.5% [Estimate]                    | 3,436   | 21.0% [Assumption]     | 722   | 570   | 36  | 50    | +8   | 40  | 508       |\n| 2030 | +5.0% [Assumption: converged to industry] | 3,608 | 21.0% [Assumption] | 758 | 599 | 37 | 52 | +8 | 42 | 534 |\nTerminal growth: 3.0% [Assumption \u2014 below long-run nominal GDP ~3.5%].\nTerminal value = 534 \u00d7 1.03 / (0.095 \u2212 0.03) = $8,462M [Arithmetic].\nPV of explicit FCFs (r=9.5%, mid-year): 429 + 390 + 383 + 370 + 355 = $1,927M.\nPV of TV: $8,462 / 1.095^4.5 = $5,638M.\nEV = $7,565M. Add net cash $360M [Estimate] \u2192 Equity = $7,925M \u2192 $285/share.\n\nEngine 2 cross-check (cycle-adjusted): mid-cycle revenue \u2248 $3.2B [Estimate], mid-cycle OPM \u2248 19\u201320% \u2192 normalized EPS \u2248 $17\u201319 [Estimate]. At a 25% discount to the 34x trailing multiple (17\u201322x), value = $300\u2013380; at mid-cycle 18x = $330 [Estimate]. Weighted final base IV: 0.7\u00d7 DCF $285 + 0.3\u00d7 normalized $330 = $300/share [Arithmetic].\n\nTornado sensitivity (key variables) [Estimate]:\n  WACC \u00b11\u03c3 (8.5%/10.5%): IV $333/$245 \u2014 VARIABLE #1.\n  FY2030 margin \u00b12pts (23%/19%): IV $365/$245 \u2014 VARIABLE #2.\n  FY2027 growth \u00b13pts (\u00b110.5%): IV $310/$270 \u2014 VARIABLE #3.\n  These three drive the thesis KPIs (Section 8).\n\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nCompetitive response: If MEDP is successful in AI-accelerated trials, IQVIA/ICON respond with price-integrated AI offerings \u2014 margin pressure within 3 years (\u20132). If MEDP stumbles, competitors hire its talent aggressively (\u20131).\nReflexivity: Negative loop active \u2014 the 16% Q1-2026 drop and litigation can impair sponsor trust (mid-trial CRO switches are rare but reputational); the high multiple had enabled cheap-EPS buybacks, which now become less effective (SBC dilution offsets).\nCustomer evolution: Medpace's sponsor base skews small/mid biopharma; as biotech funding concentrates in mega-rounds ($600M+), large sponsors may prefer one-stop generalist CROs. LTV/CAC of Medpace's niche is likely stable but the TAM shift favors breadth (\u20131).\n\nSECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nPrior (from base rates): P(fair value >$600) \u2248 20\u201325%.\nUpdate evidence: +Q2-2026 record bookings (+), +raised FY26 guidance (+), \u2212H2 implied +4.6% (\u2013), \u2212class action (\u2013), \u2212Q1-2026 0.88 book-to-bill [Unconfirmed] (\u2013). Posterior: P(FV>$600) \u2248 18\u201322%.\nScenario composition (sums to 100%):\n  Bear (25%): H2 deceleration persists; FY27 +3%; margin \u2192 18% by FY30; WACC 10.5%; IV \u2248 $190/share.\n  Base (45%): FY27 +7.5% fading to +5%; margin flat 21%; WACC 9.5%; IV \u2248 $285\u2013300/share.\n  Bull (30%): Re-acceleration to +12% in FY27; margin \u2192 23%; WACC 8.5%; IV \u2248 $418/share.\nExpected price (2-year horizon, mid-2028): 0.25\u00d7190 + 0.45\u00d7285 + 0.30\u00d7418 = $3