oking wobble temper it).\n  Total: 13/15 \u2192 VERY HIGH conviction in the SELL thesis.\nConviction decay: thesis requires confirmation within 6 months; if Q3/Q4 2026 revenue growth exceeds 10%, conviction drops 2 steps automatically. Macro headwind: \u22120.5 step already applied. Practical sizing: short position cap 4\u20136% of portfolio (see 5.5 and 6.5).\n\nSECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nShort interest: 7.81% of float; shares short 1,746,898; days to cover 4.5; MoM change \u221217.8% (short covering after Q2 beat) [Actual, aggregator]. Squeeze risk: moderate but elevated.\nInstitutional ownership: 87.47%; insider 19.75% [Actual] \u2014 founder-led alignment.\nOptions positioning: not available [Unconfirmed].\nSentiment: sell-side mean 12-mo target $581.83, median $604.5, high $692 [Actual, aggregator]. The current price is ABOVE the mean and median targets \u2014 the market is more optimistic than the Street. Contrarian-negative signal.\nCrowding risk score: 9/15 (high institutional ownership + momentum rebound + litigation controversy). Per framework: reduce position size by ~1%.\n\nSECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nMEDP as a SELL/SHORT: negative correlation with biotech funding stress; positive correlation with a market-rate shock. In a portfolio long quality compounders, this short is a partial hedge against: (a) rate-driven multiple compression, (b) biotech funding dry-up. Avoid if portfolio already net-short healthcare/tight-credit-sensitive names. As a standalone, unattractive long: expected return to fair value in 2 years is ~\u221252%.\n\nSECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nScenario-weighted expected price $301 vs T0 $620.75 \u2192 expected gross gain on short \u2248 +54% over 2 years if converged. Probability of scenario-weighted outcome being correct \u2248 55% [Estimate]; probability of >30% adverse move (bull path) \u2248 30%. Kelly fraction f* = (p\u00b7b \u2212 q\u00b7c)/b, where b=0.54, c=0.39 (loss if price goes to bull IV $418 = \u221233%); f* = (0.55\u00d70.54 \u2212 0.45\u00d70.39)/0.54 = (0.297 \u2212 0.176)/0.54 \u2248 0.22. Raw Kelly 22% \u2192 cap at framework maximum for high-conviction shorts: 6%. After crowding reduction (9/15): 5%. FINAL: 5% portfolio weight, SHORT.\n\nSECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nDownside risks to the SHORT (i.e., what drives MEDP higher):\n  \u2013 Q3/Q4-2026 revenue growth re-accelerates beyond 10% (record bookings convert).\n  \u2013 Fed cuts aggressively into a soft landing; long-duration quality re-rates higher.\n  \u2013 The class action is dismissed early, removing the governance overhang.\n  \u2013 M&A bid from a strategic acquirer at a premium to the market price.\nCatalysts for the SHORT (downside drivers):\n  \u2013 Q3-2026/H2-2026 reported growth prints near the implied ~4.6%.\n  \u2013 Motion-to-dismiss denied; discovery reveals cancellations/booking-policy details.\n  \u2013 Biotech funding disappoints in 2027; pressure on cancellations resumes.\n  \u2013 FY2027 guidance, issued with Q4-2026 results, comes in below consensus ~$3.0B.\n  \u2013 Multiple compression from 35x to 25x forward as growth decelerates.\n\nSECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nTail correlation: MEDP is a high-beta (1.15) quality compounder; in the 2022-style regime (rates up, multiples down), MEDP short correlations are favorable against long-quality portfolios. In a 2020-style liquidity crisis, shorts of ALL equities get squeezed \u2014 MEDP short would lose with everything else. CVaR (worst 5%, 3-month): +18\u201322% adverse move on the short (i.e., price to ~$735\u2013760) based on 2020/2022 analogues [Estimate]. Position cap at 5% reflects this. Common bear-trigger across a growth-long book: a surprise Fed cut would hurt this short \u2014 hedge accordingly.\n\nSECTION 8. MONITORING RULES\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nThesis-integrity thresholds (pre-defined triggers for re-evaluation):\n  1. Quarterly net book-to-bill <1.0 for two consecutive quarters \u2192 STRENGTHEN short.\n  2. Quarterly revenue YoY >+10% in Q3/Q4-2026 \u2192 CONVICTION \u22122 steps; cover half.\n  3. Cancellations > $100M in any quarter \u2192 STRENGTHEN short.\n  4. Operating margin <19% for two quarters \u2192 STRENGTHEN short.\n  5. FY2027 guidance (revenue) > $3.2B \u2192 CONVICTION \u22122 steps; re-run valuation.\n  6. Class-action motion to dismiss DENIED \u2192 CONVICTION +1 step; modest add.\n  7. Class action dismissed with prejudice \u2192 CONVICTION \u22121 step; trim.\nPre-mortem (if MEDP fails as a short and trades >$800 in 5 years, why?): (1) AI trial productivity failed to disrupt, and pricing power persisted; (2) biotech mega-rounds (2025-26) converted into a 2027-30 trial super-cycle; (3) the market permanently re-rated high-ROIC asset-light services to 40x+ amid 3% rates. Early-warning indicators: NTM backlog conversion rising above 90% of TTM revenue; monthly RFP growth >20% for four consecutive quarters; Fed dot plot signalling cuts.\n\nSECTION 9. RED TEAM \u2014 ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 9-1. Short thesis (using the same data):\n  1. H2-2026 implied growth = 4.6% YoY [Arithmetic from Actual guidance $2.845B mid \u2212 Actual H1 $1.414B \u2212 Actual H2-2025 $1.368B] \u2014 a collapse from +32.0%.\n  2. T0 price 35.3x FY2026 EPS guidance mid ($17.60) and >38x normalized FCF [Arithmetic].\n  3. Class