owngrade growth\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 9. RED TEAM\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nStep 9-1. Short thesis (5\u20137 bullets):\n1. Book-to-bill is management-adjusted: Q1 2026 was 0.88 and Q2 1.13;\n   the securities-fraud class action (Durbin v. Medpace, S.D. Ohio,\n   filed 2026-04-06 [Actual \u2014 court filing]) alleges prior understatement\n   of cancellations. The 16% single-day drop shows market distrust.\n2. P/E of 34\u00d7 trailing and 35\u00d7 forward assumes flawless execution;\n   the correct cyclically-adjusted multiple for a CRO is 15\u201320\u00d7.\n3. Small-biotech funding remains weak: PitchBook data (reported by\n   BioPharma Dive) suggests 2026 biotech VC on pace for ~$2B \u2014 flat\n   since 2022; MEDP's client base is heavily small/mid biotech.\n4. Margins are at a cyclical peak: operating margin 21.1% vs 11-year\n   median 17.4%; AI-driven productivity could compress pricing across\n   the CRO industry.\n5. CEO/founder concentration: August Troendle has deep control and a\n   litigation target; governance overhang is real.\n6. Consensus targets (mean $581.83) are BELOW the current price: the\n   sell-side is not supporting the level; momentum-only money is the\n   marginal buyer.\n7. Customer concentration in early-stage biotech = cancellations cluster\n   in downturns; FY2022 already showed a -$0.60