stitutional ownership) |\n\n**Tail Correlation (2020, 2022 analog):** In a 2022-style drawdown (rates up, biotech funding froze), MEDP underperformed growth indices because its demand is two steps away from liquidity. **Tail beta > 1.2** in that scenario. [Estimate]\n\n**Conditional VaR (95%):** Expected one-year loss in worst-case scenario = **-35% to -45%** (from current $620.75 to ~$340-400). [Estimate]\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 8 \u2014 MONITORING RULES & THESIS INTEGRITY\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**If a position is held (monitoring weight \u22642%):**\n\n| KPI | Threshold | Action |\n|---|---|---|\n| Net book-to-bill | <0.90 | Re-evaluate thesis immediately |\n| Backlog YoY growth | <0% | Downgrade to SELL |\n| Cancellation rate | >5% for 2 consecutive quarters | Downgrade to SELL |\n| Revenue growth vs guidance | <10% FY2027 | Re-evaluate |\n| Operating margin | <19% | Downgrade |\n| Q2/Q3 2026 awards | <$700M per quarter | Flag decelerating demand |\n| Litigation outcome | Settlement >$150M | Re-evaluate; cut position |\n\n**Pre-Mortem (If MEDP fails 5 years from now, why?)**\n1. **Case:** \"The bear case at $220 happened.\" Why? Biotech funding froze in 2027 after a rate-hike cycle; cancellations surged past 8%; net bookings went negative for 3 quarters. **Early warning:** book-to-bill <0.90 quarterly, cancellation rate >5%, and flat RFP counts.\n2. **Case:** \"The company won but investors lost.\" Why? The classic overpayment: business compounds at 10% but the stock fell from 35x to 20x, losing ~40%. **Early warning:** PEG > 2.5, 10Y above 5%, Fed hiking.\n3. **Case:** \"The moat eroded.\" Why? Large CROs built equivalent oncology/CNS teams; price competition pushed margins to 15%. **Early warning:** win-rate declines, RFP-to-award conversion drops, gross margin below 68%.\n\n**Decision Journal Entry (T0):**\n- T0 price: $620.75 | IV (expected): $396 | Overvalue: +57%\n- Key assumptions: 10y revenue CAGR ~6.9% (from my explicit path); margins hold 20-21%; WACC 9.4%; terminal g 3.5%.\n- Red Team concern: if the market is correctly seeing 13% growth persistence, my $620 sell is early. That possibility is captured in the bull case (25%), but does not compensate for the bear fat tail.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 9 \u2014 RED TEAM / ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 9-1. Short Thesis (5-7 bullets)**\n1. **Valuation is the strongest short:** 35x forward P/E on a company whose backlog grew only 4.9% YoY; growth must decelerate in 2027. [Actual \u2014 Q2 